1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,560
Apple's glowing logo is back.

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,350
But OLED screens have no backlight.

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,750
So how does it glow?

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,790
The secret is hidden inside the lid.

5
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,780
Behind the display sits a light source built just for the logo.

6
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:15,370
Four tiny LEDs create the entire glow.

7
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,120
iFixit found them along one edge.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,610
A reflective layer bounces their light,

9
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,800
a diffuser spreads it evenly,

10
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,880
and it shines through the whole logo.

11
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,470
The result? One evenly lit logo, with no screen backlight needed.

12
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,280
It even dims and brightens with the light in your room.

13
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,870
And one Terminal command switches it off.

